# 👻 GHOST.exe — Ghost in the Machine

> A spooky, interactive haunted terminal built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

What if your terminal could talk back?  
**GHOST.exe** is a Halloween-inspired web project where users can interact with a mysterious digital ghost, explore spooky commands, and generate random horror stories.

## ✨ Features

- 👻 Interactive ghost character with animated effects
- 💻 Retro hacker-style terminal interface
- 🔮 Commands like `summon`, `story`, `scan`, `time`, and `help`
- 📖 Randomly generated spooky stories from predefined prompts
- ⚡ Glitch animations and neon-green visuals
- 📱 Responsive design for desktop and mobile
- 🔌 Runs locally in your browser without a backend

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **HTML5** — Project structure
- **CSS3** — Styling, animations, and responsive layout
- **JavaScript** — Terminal commands and interactions

## 🚀 Getting Started

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL
```

Replace `YOUR_REPOSITORY_URL` with your actual GitHub repository URL.

### 2. Open the project

Navigate to the project folder and open `index.html` in your browser.

Alternatively, use the Live Server extension in Visual Studio Code.

### 3. Try the commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `help` | Displays available commands |
| `summon` | Contacts the fictional ghost |
| `story` | Displays a random horror story |
| `scan` | Runs a simulated system scan |
| `time` | Displays the current date and time |
| `clear` | Clears the terminal output |

## 🔓 Why Open Innovation Matters

This project explores how creative applications can run locally and remain accessible without depending on a hosted AI service.

The current version uses client-side JavaScript and predefined responses. It does **not** yet run an AI model.

A future version could integrate an open-weight language model through Ollama to generate original ghostly responses locally, improving privacy and giving developers more control over model selection and behavior.

## 🗺️ Future Improvements

- [ ] Integrate an open-weight AI model using Ollama
- [ ] Add dynamic AI-generated horror stories
